  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="DA">Right to sign language through alle stages of life</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DA">The vision of the programme is the &#x201c;right to sign language through all stages of life&#x201d;. Specifically, the programme will contribute to sustainable change towards its objective that deaf people in Vietnam, Jordan, Rwanda, Ghana, Togo, Ivory Coast and Guatemala are treated equitably and receive information, education and healthcare in their national sign language(s), ensuring full inclusion for all. This will be achieved through three pillars: 1) Organisational development, systematic and targeted advocacy work, and strengthening access to sign language training and sign language interpreting, and with the empowerment of deaf people to become leaders and advocate for the desired changes at the core. The programme&#x2019;s modus operandi is, that deaf people and their organisations undertake their roles as rights holderds and build their capacities to claim their rights and to hold the duty bearers accountable for enforcing and promoting human rights and living up to their responsibilities.</narrative>
  </description>
